WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.233 --> 00:00:08.233
Although Ash struggled against Ramos

2
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:11.466
and his Grass-type Pokémon at the Coumarine City Gym,

3
00:00:11.533 --> 00:00:15.933
our hero managed to successfully put his unique battling style to the test

4
00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:20.400
and pull off a victory, winning his fourth Kalos Gym badge!

5
00:00:24.533 --> 00:00:26.400
Hm.

6
00:00:28.233 --> 00:00:31.100
Serena from Vaniville Town, all set.

7
00:00:31.166 --> 00:00:35.466
Your entry into the Pokémon Showcase Rookie Class is complete.

8
00:00:35.533 --> 00:00:36.900
So, best of luck!

9
00:00:36.966 --> 00:00:39.133
- Wigglytuff!
- Thanks!

10
00:00:39.200 --> 00:00:40.266
- Denne!
- Hm.

11
00:00:41.966 --> 00:00:44.333
Now, Pancham? Fennekin? Ready?

12
00:00:44.400 --> 00:00:46.633
- Fenn!
- Cham!

13
00:00:47.533 --> 00:00:51.133
- It's your first performance!
- I know you're gonna be great!

14
00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.466
- Thanks a lot.
- Sure.

15
00:00:52.533 --> 00:00:56.366
I know it doesn't get underway just yet, but are you ready to go?

16
00:00:56.433 --> 00:00:59.566
Yeah, but a little bit more practice couldn't hurt.

17
00:00:59.633 --> 00:01:02.833
I have to work just as hard as Ash to be successful!

18
00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:05.033
- You're gonna do just fine.
- Pika.

19
00:01:05.099 --> 00:01:07.866
Give it all and you'll have nothing to regret.

20
00:01:07.933 --> 00:01:08.933
Right!

21
00:01:09.000 --> 00:01:10.800
♪ You're just a kid on a quest ♪

22
00:01:10.866 --> 00:01:12.566
♪ To be the best of the best ♪

23
00:01:12.633 --> 00:01:16.000
♪ Someday you're destined for power and glory ♪

24
00:01:16.066 --> 00:01:17.466
♪ You know you're up to the test ♪

25
00:01:17.533 --> 00:01:21.300
♪ There's only one way to tell this story ♪

26
00:01:21.366 --> 00:01:24.566
♪ Be a hero! Be a hero! ♪

27
00:01:24.633 --> 00:01:28.233
♪ All the power is at your command ♪

28
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:31.966
♪ Face your fears and show you're a hero ♪

29
00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:36.666
♪ The future of the world is in your hand! ♪

30
00:01:36.733 --> 00:01:38.933
♪ Pokémon! ♪

31
00:01:41.966 --> 00:01:44.800
Under The Pledging Tree!

32
00:01:51.933 --> 00:01:53.100
Huh?

33
00:01:53.166 --> 00:01:55.100
- What's all this?
- Pikachu!

34
00:01:55.166 --> 00:01:57.300
I wonder if something's going on tonight.

35
00:01:57.366 --> 00:01:59.700
They're gettin' ready for the festival.

36
00:01:59.766 --> 00:02:02.766
- Hey, Ramos!
- Wow. A festival?

37
00:02:02.833 --> 00:02:06.733
The Coumarine City Festival happens each and every year.

38
00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.166
There's a story.

39
00:02:08.233 --> 00:02:11.000
Long, long ago, there was a trainer and his Pokémon.

40
00:02:11.800 --> 00:02:16.066
They went on a journey and experienced countless adventures.

41
00:02:16.133 --> 00:02:19.366
At the end of their journey, they settled down in this land

42
00:02:19.433 --> 00:02:22.066
and lived here happily ever after.

43
00:02:22.133 --> 00:02:27.000
In honour of their lasting friendship, the trainer gave his Pokémon a little tree,

44
00:02:27.066 --> 00:02:31.400
as a lovely reminder of everything they had been through together.

45
00:02:31.466 --> 00:02:34.133
Before long, that little tree grew and grew,

46
00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:37.133
becomin' the largest tree in Coumarine City.

47
00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:40.333
And that tree is known as the Pledgin' Tree.

48
00:02:40.400 --> 00:02:42.533
Oh! That sounds wonderful!

49
00:02:42.600 --> 00:02:45.700
Hold on a second. Is that tree alive today?

50
00:02:45.766 --> 00:02:47.966
Yes. That's it over there.

51
00:02:50.166 --> 00:02:51.933
Since then, it is said,

52
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.866
if a trainer gives their Pokémon a gift while under that tree,

53
00:02:55.933 --> 00:02:58.700
the bond between them will grow even stronger.

54
00:02:58.766 --> 00:03:02.166
- It's become a tradition.
- Wow. That is just so sweet.

55
00:03:02.233 --> 00:03:06.366
- Ramos, what time does the festival begin?
- It begins at sundown.

56
00:03:06.433 --> 00:03:10.733
A trainer first places their Pokémon's present underneath the Pledgin' Tree.

57
00:03:10.800 --> 00:03:14.100
Then, the trainer offers the gift after the sun goes down.

58
00:03:14.166 --> 00:03:17.733
So that's why they're all headed toward the tree with stuff.

59
00:03:17.800 --> 00:03:20.833
Sounds like a lot of fun! Why don't we do it, too?

60
00:03:20.900 --> 00:03:21.833
Pika! Pancham!

61
00:03:21.900 --> 00:03:24.200
That's great! It sounds like a lot of fun!

62
00:03:24.266 --> 00:03:26.933
Heh! I wonder what I should give?

63
00:03:27.000 --> 00:03:29.266
I wanna give a present, too!

64
00:03:29.333 --> 00:03:32.500
Good! I'm on my way to go and decorate the tree now.

65
00:03:32.566 --> 00:03:35.466
Great! I'm so glad you told us.

66
00:03:35.533 --> 00:03:38.833
Guys, now that we know, we'd better go buy those presents!

67
00:03:38.900 --> 00:03:42.833
Hey, there's a street known for its shopping right near the port.

68
00:03:42.900 --> 00:03:46.866
Why don't we go there? I'm sure that we'll find whatever we need.

69
00:03:46.933 --> 00:03:49.033
Good idea. What do you say?

70
00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.300
I'm going to do something different.

71
00:03:51.366 --> 00:03:53.200
I'm off to the Pokémon Centre.

72
00:03:53.266 --> 00:03:56.333
- I know what you're up to.
- I'll bet you do.

73
00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:59.033
I'm going to assemble my present by hand.

74
00:03:59.100 --> 00:04:02.600
Sounds cool. I'm sure your Pokémon will like that best.

75
00:04:02.666 --> 00:04:05.566
- You're right!
- Make sure you don't blow anything up.

76
00:04:05.633 --> 00:04:09.433
Come on! Bonnie, my inventions don't always blow up, you know!

77
00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:14.933
- Wait for me here, OK, Pikachu?
- Pika?

78
00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.633
I know they all love surprises.

79
00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:19.966
Presents are more fun when you don't know what you're getting.

80
00:04:20.033 --> 00:04:21.500
You're right! Good idea.

81
00:04:23.300 --> 00:04:25.766
Will you stay here and wait for me, too?

82
00:04:25.833 --> 00:04:28.533
I'm gonna find you something really nice.

83
00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:29.900
- Fenne.
- Cham-cham.

84
00:04:29.966 --> 00:04:32.833
So can I take care of them while you're gone?

85
00:04:32.900 --> 00:04:34.833
Yeah, that'd be great, Bonnie.

86
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:36.633
Yay! Leave it to me!

87
00:04:36.700 --> 00:04:39.633
Come on out, everybody!

88
00:04:41.766 --> 00:04:44.900
You just relax and wait while we get your presents.

89
00:04:45.866 --> 00:04:47.900
OK, Bonnie, it's up to you.

90
00:04:47.966 --> 00:04:50.600
- Have fun taking care of them.
- OK!

91
00:04:50.666 --> 00:04:54.300
Since I'll be making my presents, I can help Bonnie watch them too.

92
00:04:54.366 --> 00:04:56.366
We're gonna have a great time!

93
00:04:56.433 --> 00:04:59.200
You all come out as well!

94
00:05:00.700 --> 00:05:04.733
- Denne-ne!
- OK, ready? Follow me!

95
00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:10.233
- Ready to go?
- Mm-hm.

96
00:05:11.433 --> 00:05:14.366
Wow. Ash and I are all alone.

97
00:05:14.433 --> 00:05:18.100
It's... it's almost like we're out on a date!

98
00:05:18.166 --> 00:05:22.266
- What are you gonna get, Serena?
- I'm not really sure yet.

99
00:05:22.333 --> 00:05:26.100
Isn't that sweet? They're getting presents for their Pokémon.

100
00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:29.833
Yes. Knowing those twerps, I'm certain they'll find something

101
00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:31.900
that will make their Pokémon jump for joy!

102
00:05:31.966 --> 00:05:35.866
So if we swipe those Pokémon and their presents, guess what?

103
00:05:35.933 --> 00:05:37.900
Our name will soon be in lights!

104
00:05:37.966 --> 00:05:41.733
- While the Boss walks us down easy street!
- Wobbuffet!

105
00:05:45.566 --> 00:05:46.966
Whoa!

106
00:05:47.033 --> 00:05:49.800
- It's beautiful!
- Awesome!

107
00:05:51.000 --> 00:05:53.533
Ah!

108
00:05:56.966 --> 00:06:00.300
This is the heart of the shopping district.

109
00:06:00.366 --> 00:06:03.166
I think we should go check out every store.

110
00:06:03.233 --> 00:06:05.033
Sounds good.

111
00:06:06.333 --> 00:06:08.766
Look at how cute this is!

112
00:06:08.833 --> 00:06:10.266
- Serena!
- Huh?

113
00:06:10.333 --> 00:06:15.100
Check out this awesome face! Do you think Pikachu and the others will like it?

114
00:06:15.166 --> 00:06:17.900
- It might be the tiniest bit too big.
- Huh?

115
00:06:17.966 --> 00:06:20.300
Now that you mention it, you're right.

116
00:06:21.366 --> 00:06:23.533
Hey, Ash!

117
00:06:23.600 --> 00:06:25.033
- Ash?
- Serena!

118
00:06:25.100 --> 00:06:28.566
Look at this cool hat. So, what do you think?

119
00:06:28.633 --> 00:06:31.800
- Nice. But who's gonna wear that?
- You're right.

120
00:06:35.033 --> 00:06:37.500
Ash, this shop has some nice things!

121
00:06:37.566 --> 00:06:38.833
- Come take a look.
- Hey, Serena!

122
00:06:38.900 --> 00:06:43.266
I'm gonna check out that store! I'll meet you back at the station!

123
00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:45.800
Uh, wait! Do you have to go so soon?

124
00:06:45.866 --> 00:06:48.700
Oh...

125
00:06:52.166 --> 00:06:54.033
Huh? Ah!

126
00:06:54.100 --> 00:06:57.033
It's adorable!

127
00:06:57.100 --> 00:07:02.100
You know, if I wore an outfit like this at the Showcase...

128
00:07:03.500 --> 00:07:04.666
OK!

129
00:07:04.733 --> 00:07:07.600
I want everybody to get in line so I can brush you!

130
00:07:07.666 --> 00:07:09.733
- Pan!
- Pika!

131
00:07:09.800 --> 00:07:11.100
Frog. Frog.

132
00:07:11.166 --> 00:07:14.066
- Cha-ha! Cha...
- Bunnelby! By!

133
00:07:14.133 --> 00:07:17.233
Come on, Hawlucha and Bunnelby, get in line, too!

134
00:07:17.300 --> 00:07:20.200
I know! Serena made Poké Puffs,

135
00:07:20.266 --> 00:07:22.966
so that means we can all have snack time afterwards!

136
00:07:23.033 --> 00:07:24.266
- Hawlucha.
- Bunnelby.

137
00:07:24.333 --> 00:07:26.533
Everybody get in line.

138
00:07:26.600 --> 00:07:27.933
Hm.

139
00:07:28.000 --> 00:07:31.133
Huh? What's wrong, Goomy? You look sick.

140
00:07:31.200 --> 00:07:34.633
You need water now! Water! Water!

141
00:07:40.033 --> 00:07:41.300
My!

142
00:07:41.366 --> 00:07:43.533
Thank goodness.

143
00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.600
- Pancham. Pan-pan!
- Chespin.

144
00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:50.566
Che! Che! Chespin...

145
00:07:50.633 --> 00:07:53.366
- Come on! No fighting!
- Pika, pika.

146
00:07:53.433 --> 00:07:56.233
Wow. Watching them sure is a lot of work.

147
00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.300
Chespin! Pancham! Be nice to each other!

148
00:08:00.300 --> 00:08:02.533
So, what am I gonna get them?

149
00:08:02.600 --> 00:08:04.866
Maybe something that'll come in handy in a battle.

150
00:08:04.933 --> 00:08:07.600
Say, are you looking for a Pokémon gift?

151
00:08:07.666 --> 00:08:09.866
- How about one of these Macho Braces?
- No...

152
00:08:09.933 --> 00:08:11.666
- Hold on. Or a rocky helmet?
- Uh...

153
00:08:11.733 --> 00:08:14.966
- A substitute plush?
- Wait. Will you hold on for a sec?

154
00:08:15.033 --> 00:08:17.500
A sprinkler tap?

155
00:08:17.566 --> 00:08:19.500
- Aaah!
- Gah. Whoopsie.

156
00:08:20.466 --> 00:08:23.500
Whoa, I'm stumped. What do I get?

157
00:08:26.466 --> 00:08:29.466
Man, oh, man.

158
00:08:31.400 --> 00:08:36.900
Wow. Who knew this would be so hard? I've gotta get something.

159
00:08:36.966 --> 00:08:39.200
Thank you for your help!

160
00:08:40.400 --> 00:08:42.733
There. Mission accomplished!

161
00:08:42.799 --> 00:08:45.300
Now I hope they like them.

162
00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:48.900
Sorry to keep you waiting!

163
00:08:50.033 --> 00:08:53.600
- So, did you get 'em something good?
- Mm-hm. I did!

164
00:08:53.666 --> 00:08:56.533
And I think I'm gonna decorate them myself.

165
00:08:56.600 --> 00:08:59.366
- Wait. Where's yours?
- I couldn't find a thing.

166
00:08:59.433 --> 00:09:02.333
- I'm sorry to hear that.
- We've still got time.

167
00:09:02.400 --> 00:09:05.200
We'll just relax and find something great.

168
00:09:05.266 --> 00:09:06.900
You bet. Nice and easy.

169
00:09:06.966 --> 00:09:09.633
- Huh?

170
00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:12.000
Congratulations!

171
00:09:12.066 --> 00:09:15.100
Who's that Pokémon?

172
00:09:19.133 --> 00:09:20.966
It's Dunsparce!

173
00:09:21.033 --> 00:09:23.666
Dunsparce!

174
00:09:25.133 --> 00:09:27.000
- Ah! Huh?
- You did it!

175
00:09:27.066 --> 00:09:30.966
You have the distinct honour of being our one millionth customer!

176
00:09:31.033 --> 00:09:32.200
Who, me?

177
00:09:32.266 --> 00:09:35.033
- Give this young man a round of applause!
- Wow!

178
00:09:35.100 --> 00:09:36.800
- Congratulations.
- Thank you.

179
00:09:36.866 --> 00:09:40.133
To commemorate this occasion, please accept this gift.

180
00:09:40.200 --> 00:09:43.066
Hey, thanks a lot. Really.

181
00:09:44.333 --> 00:09:48.033
I never expected I'd be the one to get a gift.

182
00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:52.800
What did they give you? Please, show me. Ash, come on!

183
00:09:54.600 --> 00:09:57.333
- Huh?
- Wow! That's such a pretty ribbon!

184
00:09:57.400 --> 00:10:01.900
Yeah. But I still have to get a present for all my Pokémon.

185
00:10:01.966 --> 00:10:04.933
I forgot all about that.

186
00:10:05.000 --> 00:10:08.300
Pikachu and the others will love anything you choose.

187
00:10:08.366 --> 00:10:11.233
All they care about is that the gift comes from you.

188
00:10:11.300 --> 00:10:12.666
- You think?
- Sure!

189
00:10:12.733 --> 00:10:15.033
What would make you happy if you got a gift?

190
00:10:15.100 --> 00:10:17.700
Make me happy? Does it matter?

191
00:10:17.766 --> 00:10:20.700
Yeah. Because they're your Pokémon.

192
00:10:20.766 --> 00:10:22.800
And they think just like you do.

193
00:10:22.866 --> 00:10:28.100
Think like I do. What would make me happy?

194
00:10:28.166 --> 00:10:31.466
That's it, Serena! That's it!

195
00:10:31.533 --> 00:10:33.366
Huh?

196
00:10:36.866 --> 00:10:40.200
- Thanks a lot! Later!
- Huh? Ash?

197
00:10:40.266 --> 00:10:44.100
I've got somewhere to go! I'll meet you back at the Pokémon Centre!

198
00:10:44.166 --> 00:10:47.100
Huh? Somewhere? Where, where?

199
00:10:50.900 --> 00:10:53.333
All right, let's do this!

200
00:11:00.266 --> 00:11:02.333
- Kin?
- Hi. I'm back.

201
00:11:02.400 --> 00:11:04.033
- Fenn, fenn, fenn!
- Hi, Serena.

202
00:11:04.100 --> 00:11:07.166
- Huh? But I thought Ash went with you.
- Kin!

203
00:11:07.233 --> 00:11:12.600
He's still looking for a present. But I think he got a great idea.

204
00:11:12.666 --> 00:11:14.700
-Hi, everyone!

205
00:11:14.766 --> 00:11:16.366
Bonnie, thanks for looking after them.

206
00:11:16.433 --> 00:11:20.733
Sure thing. It was a lot of fun. Except...

207
00:11:20.800 --> 00:11:24.166
- Bonnie? What's the matter?
- It's just...

208
00:11:24.233 --> 00:11:27.066
I wanna give everyone a present, too!

209
00:11:27.133 --> 00:11:29.600
But do I have to be a trainer?

210
00:11:29.666 --> 00:11:35.500
Bonnie! Mm-mm. Of course you don't! I'm sure everyone would love it.

211
00:11:35.566 --> 00:11:36.600
Fennekin!

212
00:11:37.966 --> 00:11:39.500
- Pika, Pika!
- Denne-ne!

213
00:11:39.566 --> 00:11:41.400
You mean it?

214
00:11:41.466 --> 00:11:44.300
'Kay, then I'll make a drawing of all of you.

215
00:11:44.366 --> 00:11:47.900
- That'll be my present.
- Pika!

216
00:11:47.966 --> 00:11:50.033
Now line up! OK?

217
00:11:50.100 --> 00:11:53.266
Denne-ne-ne-ne-ne-ne!

218
00:11:53.333 --> 00:11:56.033
Nobody move.

219
00:11:56.100 --> 00:12:00.100
I know it'll make a wonderful present. OK, time to get to work.

220
00:12:00.166 --> 00:12:03.066
Right! I had better get busy, too.

221
00:12:06.266 --> 00:12:09.100
Huh? Maybe I should find just a little bit more.

222
00:12:09.166 --> 00:12:10.200
-Huh?

223
00:12:10.266 --> 00:12:13.266
Dunsparce!

224
00:12:13.333 --> 00:12:16.133
A Dunsparce? Never thought I'd find one here!

225
00:12:16.200 --> 00:12:18.633
- I think I'll catch you! Huh?
- Dun...

226
00:12:18.700 --> 00:12:23.300
- Aah! I don't have any Poké Balls!
- Dunsparce!

227
00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.633
No, wait. I can't let this thing get me down right now!

228
00:12:36.233 --> 00:12:39.633
- It's beautiful!
- So pretty!

229
00:12:39.700 --> 00:12:43.833
It looks like the decorations for the festival are all ready to go!

230
00:12:43.900 --> 00:12:47.400
- Pika, pi!
- Ash, finally! Where have you been?

231
00:12:47.466 --> 00:12:52.500
- It took a little longer than I thought.
- So, Ash, did you find a present?

232
00:12:52.566 --> 00:12:54.466
Yup!

233
00:12:54.533 --> 00:12:55.833
- Hi.
- Pika, pi.

234
00:13:03.233 --> 00:13:04.733
- Ramos.
- Huh?

235
00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:08.300
- Good. You're all here.
- Right!

236
00:13:08.366 --> 00:13:10.966
You can put your presents over there.

237
00:13:14.566 --> 00:13:16.233
Hm.

238
00:13:16.300 --> 00:13:18.400
Huh?

239
00:13:20.466 --> 00:13:24.233
- What happens next?
- I imagine we'll find out soon enough.

240
00:13:24.300 --> 00:13:26.066
Let's begin.

241
00:13:30.333 --> 00:13:33.566
- Oh, no! What a way to start!

242
00:13:34.666 --> 00:13:37.833
- Aaah!
- Ramos, what's going on?

243
00:13:37.900 --> 00:13:41.466
- Aah!
- Frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog, frog.

244
00:13:41.533 --> 00:13:42.900
Frogadier!

245
00:13:47.700 --> 00:13:49.033
What's the meanin' of this?

246
00:13:49.100 --> 00:13:51.766
Prepare for trouble, the meaning's quite clear!

247
00:13:51.833 --> 00:13:54.033
We steal your presents and fill you with fear!

248
00:13:54.100 --> 00:13:56.533
To protect the world from devastation!

249
00:13:56.600 --> 00:13:59.400
To unite all people within our nation!

250
00:13:59.466 --> 00:14:02.566
To denounce the evils of twerps hoarding gifts!

251
00:14:02.633 --> 00:14:05.100
To extend and teach the virtues of thrift!

252
00:14:06.066 --> 00:14:08.333
- Jessie!
- And James.

253
00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:11.266
Team Rocket blasts off at the speed of light!

254
00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:14.166
Surrender now or prepare for a festival fight!

255
00:14:14.233 --> 00:14:17.866
- Meowth, that's right!
- Wobbuffet!

256
00:14:18.966 --> 00:14:21.266
Team Rocket, what are you doing here?

257
00:14:21.333 --> 00:14:24.600
- I want my drawing back right now!
- Silence, twerps!

258
00:14:24.666 --> 00:14:27.400
These presents are now part of the Team Rocket Festival!

259
00:14:27.466 --> 00:14:31.500
And when combined with your Pokémon, we'll have caught a cornucopia caché!

260
00:14:31.566 --> 00:14:35.766
Yeah, whatever that means. Time to clean.

261
00:14:38.266 --> 00:14:40.200
- Gogoat, ready?
- Hmm.

262
00:14:40.266 --> 00:14:41.200
Ramos!

263
00:14:41.266 --> 00:14:43.433
Leave everything to us, OK?

264
00:14:43.500 --> 00:14:45.333
Right! It's all yours!

265
00:14:45.400 --> 00:14:48.333
OK, Pikachu. Use Iron Tail!

266
00:14:48.466 --> 00:14:51.366
Chu! Aah, Pikachu!

267
00:14:53.766 --> 00:14:54.833
Oof!

268
00:14:54.900 --> 00:14:58.733
Grr! Why, you impertinent party-poopers!

269
00:14:58.800 --> 00:15:03.366
Look! We put a lot of time into getting those gifts! So quit while you're ahead!

270
00:15:03.433 --> 00:15:05.133
You're way behind, twerp!

271
00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:07.566
Pumpkaboo, Shadow Ball!

272
00:15:07.633 --> 00:15:09.500
Pump-ka-ka-ka-ka-ka-boo!

273
00:15:09.566 --> 00:15:12.033
Frogadier, use Water Pulse!

274
00:15:12.100 --> 00:15:15.366
Frog! Frogadier!

275
00:15:16.466 --> 00:15:18.333
Inkay, use Psybeam!

276
00:15:20.133 --> 00:15:21.866
Inkay!

277
00:15:21.933 --> 00:15:24.066
Bunnelby! Mud Shot, let's go!

278
00:15:24.133 --> 00:15:27.000
Bunnelby!

279
00:15:28.233 --> 00:15:31.300
- Fennekin, use Flamethrower!
- Fennekin!

280
00:15:31.366 --> 00:15:35.700
- Pikachu, Thunderbolt!
- Pikachu!

281
00:15:35.766 --> 00:15:37.666
Now, Chespin, Pin Missile!

282
00:15:37.733 --> 00:15:40.566
Chespin!

283
00:15:40.633 --> 00:15:43.866
- Already?

284
00:15:43.933 --> 00:15:45.800
We're blasting off prematurely!

285
00:15:45.866 --> 00:15:49.500
- Wobbuffet!
- Inkay!

286
00:15:51.800 --> 00:15:54.633
What a relief. The presents are safe and sound.

287
00:15:54.700 --> 00:15:58.066
- That includes your drawing.
- My drawing's all right!

288
00:15:58.133 --> 00:15:59.466
Here you go.

289
00:15:59.533 --> 00:16:01.566
What a relief! It didn't break.

290
00:16:01.633 --> 00:16:03.566
- Is this one yours?
- Yeah.

291
00:16:03.633 --> 00:16:06.566
Whose is this?

292
00:16:06.633 --> 00:16:09.766
- Here you go. Thank you.
- Mm-hm.

293
00:16:09.833 --> 00:16:11.866
Back to where we started.

294
00:16:11.933 --> 00:16:15.066
To strengthen the bond between trainer and Pokémon,

295
00:16:15.133 --> 00:16:18.866
let us begin our beloved annual festival as we all gather here

296
00:16:18.933 --> 00:16:20.533
beneath the Pledgin' Tree.

297
00:16:20.600 --> 00:16:22.666
Now, it's time for the countdown!

298
00:16:22.733 --> 00:16:26.666
- Five, four, and three, and two...
- Pika, pika...

299
00:16:26.733 --> 00:16:28.933
- And one!
- Pika!

300
00:16:38.133 --> 00:16:41.000
- Wow, beautiful!
- Totally awesome!

301
00:16:41.066 --> 00:16:42.933
-So sparkly!

302
00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.500
It's like a tower of light!

303
00:16:50.933 --> 00:16:54.733
What do you think? It looks just like you guys, right?

304
00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:57.466
-Denne!

305
00:16:57.533 --> 00:17:00.566
Ta-da! The ribbon's for Fennekin,

306
00:17:00.633 --> 00:17:02.833
and the sunglasses are for Pancham.

307
00:17:02.900 --> 00:17:06.633
I did the decorations myself!

308
00:17:06.700 --> 00:17:09.633
- Nekin!
- Cham.

309
00:17:09.700 --> 00:17:13.200
Here, this ribbon is actually a wind-up key.

310
00:17:13.266 --> 00:17:16.000
If you put it in here and turn it like so...

311
00:17:18.833 --> 00:17:22.633
It's a Clemontic Gear mini-music box!

312
00:17:22.700 --> 00:17:24.900
And I made little versions of you!

313
00:17:28.433 --> 00:17:31.200
There we go. I handpicked these berries.

314
00:17:32.433 --> 00:17:36.933
I got a ton. So you guys can eat as much as you want to!

315
00:17:48.366 --> 00:17:50.533
I'm not having a good time!

316
00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:52.700
So close and yet so far.

317
00:17:52.766 --> 00:17:54.366
Close doesn't count.

318
00:17:54.433 --> 00:17:57.700
Huh? Look what I found. A present in the tree.

319
00:17:57.766 --> 00:18:00.700
- Oh, that one's for you.
- Eh?

320
00:18:00.766 --> 00:18:04.233
- And this? For Inkay.
- These are for Wobbuffet and Pumpkaboo.

321
00:18:04.300 --> 00:18:06.966
- Inkay, Inkay.
- Kaboo.

322
00:18:07.033 --> 00:18:09.200
Wobba. Wobba.

323
00:18:09.266 --> 00:18:12.666
Well, after all, you do help us from time to time.

324
00:18:12.733 --> 00:18:15.200
Tokens of our sincere love and affection.

325
00:18:15.266 --> 00:18:18.000
You lugs!

326
00:18:19.800 --> 00:18:22.966
- Wait, it's dangerous!
- Not you too. It won't hold!

327
00:18:23.033 --> 00:18:24.833
Are you out of your mind?

328
00:18:29.600 --> 00:18:32.900
- It's for you. Thanks for all your help.
- Wigglytuff!

329
00:18:32.966 --> 00:18:34.700
- By!
- Lux!

330
00:18:34.766 --> 00:18:37.900
- Chespin.
- I'm so glad that you all like it. Huh?

331
00:18:37.966 --> 00:18:40.166
Tastes pretty good, huh, Dedenne?

332
00:18:40.233 --> 00:18:42.900
- Denne-ne!
- Cham! Pan!

333
00:18:42.966 --> 00:18:44.900
Hmm.

334
00:18:44.966 --> 00:18:47.700
Wow! You both look so good wearing those!

335
00:18:47.766 --> 00:18:49.333
- Fennekin.
- Cham.

336
00:18:49.400 --> 00:18:52.733
You'll be amazing in the Pokémon Showcase!

337
00:18:52.800 --> 00:18:55.433
Hold on. Who is that for? Fenne.

338
00:18:56.600 --> 00:18:59.866
- Do you think someone forgot to give it?
- Huh?

339
00:19:02.366 --> 00:19:04.800
The card says "To Serena".

340
00:19:04.866 --> 00:19:07.300
What do you know? This present's for you!

341
00:19:07.366 --> 00:19:09.833
- Open it. Open it!
- Sure.

342
00:19:12.066 --> 00:19:13.500
-Pika.

343
00:19:13.566 --> 00:19:16.200
A dress! It's so pretty!

344
00:19:16.266 --> 00:19:18.800
Ah! But how?

345
00:19:18.866 --> 00:19:21.366
I'm glad you finally got that package.

346
00:19:21.433 --> 00:19:23.833
It was delivered to the Pokémon Centre for you.

347
00:19:23.900 --> 00:19:26.166
- Pokémon Centre?
- Right.

348
00:19:26.233 --> 00:19:29.000
It arrived with instructions to give it to you

349
00:19:29.066 --> 00:19:32.466
- in a way that would be a big surprise.
- Huh?

350
00:19:32.533 --> 00:19:35.366
- Do you like it?
- Oh, Mom.

351
00:19:35.433 --> 00:19:39.033
I figured if you were going to enter the Pokémon Showcase,

352
00:19:39.100 --> 00:19:40.700
you'd want a brand-new outfit.

353
00:19:40.766 --> 00:19:41.800
I was right!

354
00:19:41.866 --> 00:19:42.966
You were.

355
00:19:43.033 --> 00:19:46.000
You never like any of the outfits I pick out for you,

356
00:19:46.066 --> 00:19:47.666
so I tried something different.

357
00:19:47.733 --> 00:19:51.100
- I chose the dress I didn't like.
- Oh, that's so sweet!

358
00:19:51.166 --> 00:19:54.100
I know you'll be amazing. Good luck.

359
00:19:54.166 --> 00:19:56.600
Thanks.

360
00:19:58.900 --> 00:20:00.833
- Huh?

361
00:20:02.000 --> 00:20:03.566
Fireworks!

362
00:20:03.633 --> 00:20:05.766
Pikachu.

363
00:20:07.600 --> 00:20:09.566
- Serena?
- What, Ash?

364
00:20:09.633 --> 00:20:13.733
Here. Take this. I wanted you to have something from me.

365
00:20:13.800 --> 00:20:17.400
- But what for?
- I never would've been able

366
00:20:17.466 --> 00:20:19.866
to choose a present for them without your help.

367
00:20:19.933 --> 00:20:23.366
So this is just my way of saying thanks a lot.

368
00:20:23.433 --> 00:20:28.866
Thank you, Ash. I'll always treasure it.

369
00:20:31.433 --> 00:20:34.566
With a little assistance from our heroes,

370
00:20:34.633 --> 00:20:38.333
the festival celebrating the bond between trainer and Pokémon

371
00:20:38.400 --> 00:20:40.900
is safe, secure, and underway.

372
00:20:40.966 --> 00:20:44.066
Before long, Serena's first Pokémon Showcase

373
00:20:44.133 --> 00:20:48.800
will be underway too, as the journey continues!
